<name>Meter &amp; Gauge System</name>
<para id="RM0000005A800RX" category="J" type-id="300N7" name-id="630WV-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Water Temperature Receiver Gauge Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005A800RX_04" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000B6200000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The combination meter assembly receives the engine coolant temperature signal from the engine control computer via CAN communication. The combination meter assembly drives the water temperature receiver gauge based on the received engine coolant temperature signal.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>The engine coolant temperature indication is greatly affected by the condition of the engine. This flowchart is designed for diagnosis on the assumption that there is no malfunction on the engine side. Before performing the inspection according to this flowchart, check that there is no malfunction in the engine. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="X39400000QQ017D"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005A800RX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000005I00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162457J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005A800RX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000B6300000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>Before performing the inspection according to this flowchart, check that there is no malfunction in the engine. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="X39400000QQ017D"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
